{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152726-what-other-fellowships-would-you-like-to-see","id":1152726,"title":"What other Fellowships would you like to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-24T23:34:16-07:00","id":1152726,"title":"What other Fellowships would you like to see?","content":"Say we live in a perfect, blessed world where Dark Ages: Mage gets more content. What other Fellowships would you want to see, beyond the handful of canon ones?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T01:40:52-07:00","id":1152731,"title":"","content":"The Akashics would be a good one","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T02:34:58-07:00","id":1152735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152726-what-other-fellowships-would-you-like-to-see?p=1152731#post1152731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Akashics would be a good one</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially given that &quot;Guide to the Traditions&quot; reveals that the Akashics are the oldest pre-council Tradition/Fellowship, in the way that they existed as an organized group long before the others did.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In truth, the oldest of the eleven factions that<br /> have claimed membership in the Council of Nine<br /> is the Akashayana Sangha \u2014 known to Westerners<br /> as the Akashic Brotherhood. Founded in Tibet, the<br /> Brotherhood has existed as a single, slowly growing<br /> sect for at least 6000 years.<br /> &lt;...&gt; For those that care about such things, the birth<br /> order of the remaining Traditions are: Ahl-i-Batin<br /> (500 BC); Order of Hermes (AD 767); Euthanatoi<br /> (1314); Solificati (1315); Verbena (1440); Cult of<br /> Ecstasy (1443); Celestial Chorus and Dreamspeakers<br /> (both approximately 1452); Sons of Ether (1806);<br /> Virtual Adepts (1823). </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T07:07:13-07:00","id":1152794,"title":"","content":"I would enjoy seeing European fellowships made up of the Dionysian and Thanatoic groups that would eventually help form the Cult of Ecstasy and Euthanatoi. <br /> <br /> <br /> (But then my idea Mage: The Dark Ages setting would've involved the Craftmasons, Voices of Mercy, European Subtle Ones, Gardeners of the Tree, Keepers of the Sacred Flame, Memento Mori, and Christian Ecstatic heretics, with the Houses of Hermes as their own stand alone sub-game/setting.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-25T18:06:04-07:00","id":1152993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152726-what-other-fellowships-would-you-like-to-see?p=1152794#post1152794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> with the Houses of Hermes as their own stand alone sub-game/setting.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Perhaps we could call it the Art of Magic?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T03:20:40-07:00","id":1153097,"title":"","content":"An interesting Fellowship to consider and include in a new MtA: DA book would be the True Mages who would later become part of the Traditions' Cult of Ecstasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-26-2017, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T05:33:03-07:00","id":1153129,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152726-what-other-fellowships-would-you-like-to-see?p=1152993#post1152993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Perhaps we could call it the Art of Magic?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, no. It needs to be fancier. Maybe if we put it in Latin \u2026.<br /> <br /> <br /> More seriously, my thought was that you have the other seven Fellowships as being very loosely aligned to help each other stave off both the long standing heavy handedness of the Pax Hermetica/Houses of Hermes (who have only gotten worse since they found out the Tremere have betrayed them and have started picking fights with all vampires, making things worse for all mages) and the increasingly dangerous Order of Pure Thought &amp; True Faith/Gabrielites and their forthcoming Illuminated Inquisition (not to be confused with the Society of Leopold's Shadow Inquisition or the real world Papal Inquisition).<br /> The M:tDA Companion would've had a chapter on the Houses of Hermes, one on the Web of Faith, one on the Gabrielites, one about minor European factions, and one about Mages in 12th or 13th century Africa, India, and China (and maybe Mesoamerica).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":12890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","user":"No One of Consequence","date":". 10-26-2017, 08:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T06:55:34-07:00","id":1153147,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I'm more interested in different or additional Pillars than I am in more Fellowships. <br /> <br /> I'd like a set of Pillars for the Old Faith that doesn't seem so narrowly focused on one small part of them. Perhaps that could be accomplished by breaking down the Old Faith into sub-Fellowships with different Pillars for each.<br /> <br /> I'd like more Pillars for the Order of Hermes. They are the Fellowship best able to assimilate external magicks into their own Hermetic systems and thus should have the greatest diversity of options. At minimum, Materia should be available to all Hermetics, and some sort of Correspondence-analog is needed too. (I have a custom version that is two-thirds Correspondence and one-third Spirit lying around.) If you wanted to go even deeper, specific Houses should have unique Pillars: something Fae-related for Merinita, something Time-related for Criamon, etc.<br /> <br /> The Valdaermen need a Pillar focused on death; they do by far the most necromancy out of all the Fellowships, but none of their existing Pillars specifically focus on it, and the rotes we're given that include raising the dead don't seem to fit within their component Pillars. (I haven't come up with a custom one for this yet.)<br /> <br /> The Messianic Voices need their Pillars switched around so the powers associated with them actually make a lick of sense. (I proposed these changes in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/899958-aren-t-the-da-m-archangel-pillars-all-wrong\">this thread</a>.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T07:06:21-07:00","id":1153157,"title":"","content":"Was there some sort of guideline for creating new Pillars in the Grimoure/Companion? I can't recall.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-26T10:38:02-07:00","id":1153220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152726-what-other-fellowships-would-you-like-to-see?p=1153157#post1153157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was there some sort of guideline for creating new Pillars in the Grimoure/Companion? I can't recall.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it focused on the mechanical details. The harder part of custom Pillars, in my experience, is tying them to the real-world lore.<br /> <br /> Coming up with the reworked Messianic Voices Pillars was relatively easy for me as I was raised Catholic and am familiar with a lot of the real-world stories involving those angelic figures. Coming up with my Correspondence/Spirit Pillar was a lot harder because I don't know much about Hermeticism.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7356-haldir2012","name":"haldir2012","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"148"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-27T09:08:27-07:00","id":1153495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haldir2012</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1152726-what-other-fellowships-would-you-like-to-see?p=1153220#post1153220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it focused on the mechanical details. The harder part of custom Pillars, in my experience, is tying them to the real-world lore.<br /> <br /> Coming up with the reworked Messianic Voices Pillars was relatively easy for me as I was raised Catholic and am familiar with a lot of the real-world stories involving those angelic figures. Coming up with my Correspondence/Spirit Pillar was a lot harder because I don't know much about Hermeticism.</div> </div> </div> </div>In sense that word is used commonly and specifically in Mage, neither did the members of the Dark Ages Order of Hermes. That's stuff that started in the Renaissance and wasn't even on the radar in the later part of the Dark Ages. Using Hermeticism for the DA Order of Hermes is like using the terminology and thought processes of modern chemical engineering for Enlightenment alchemists IF you were playing a game set in the 17th century. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}